  ("Is the Ontario heat pump rebate still available in 2026?", "Yes. As of our last check the Home Renovation Savings Program is accepting heat pump applications in 2026. The program has not published a fixed end date and can change or close when funding is used up, so we recommend getting pre-approved sooner rather than later."),
  ("How much is the heat pump rebate in Ontario?", "Up to $7,500 for a cold-climate air-source heat pump in a home heated by electricity, oil, propane or wood, calculated by heat pump size. Homes heated with Enbridge natural gas qualify for a smaller tier, commonly up to $2,000. Ground-source heat pumps can receive up to $12,000."),
  ("Do I have to get pre-approved before installing a heat pump?", "Yes. Pre-approval must be granted before installation. A heat pump installed before approval is not eligible for the rebate. EHI submits the pre-approval for you and schedules the install only after it's confirmed."),
  ("Which heat pumps qualify for the Ontario rebate?", "The heat pump must be a cold-climate air-source model listed on Natural Resources Canada's qualified products list and installed by a participating contractor. Midea EVOX G3 and selected Kepler and Lennox models we install are on that list; we confirm the exact model number before pre-approval."),
  ("Can I get the heat pump rebate as a senior or low-income household?", "The Home Renovation Savings Program is not income-tested, so seniors and lower-income homeowners qualify under the same rules as everyone else. Some local utilities and municipalities run extra programs; we'll point you to any that apply in your area."),
  ("How long does it take to get the rebate money?", "Timelines are set by the program and vary with application volume. Payment typically follows final document submission within a few weeks to a couple of months. We submit everything promptly after install so your file isn't the one holding things up."),
  ("Is there a furnace rebate in Ontario?", "There is no stand-alone gas furnace rebate under the Home Renovation Savings Program. The heat pump rebate is the main HVAC incentive, and pairing a heat pump with a new high-efficiency furnace as a hybrid system lets you claim the heat pump portion."),
